# parthmaru.com project rule

This is Parth Maru's personal portfolio and technical publishing website.

Before significant implementation or design work, use these repository documents as the source of truth:

- @docs/PROJECT.md
- @docs/DESIGN.md
- @docs/HOMEPAGE.md
- @docs/CONTENT.md
- @docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
- @docs/DECISIONS.md
- @docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

The approved homepage visual reference is `mockups/homepage-final.png`.

Documentation is product law. The mockup is visual direction. Mockup copy is illustrative unless confirmed in the docs or provided by Parth.

## Non-negotiable product rules

- Build the MVP, not hypothetical future infrastructure.
- Top-level navigation is Home, Projects, Writing, About.
- Use `PM` as the navbar mark. Do not repeat `Parth Maru` beside it.
- The full name appears prominently in the hero.
- Social links belong in the footer.
- No top-level Notes section in the MVP.
- No top-level Build Log section in the MVP.
- BugTracker is the initial featured project and must not be duplicated immediately beside itself as a recent project.
- Do not invent sections, content, achievements, dates, metrics, technologies, or social URLs.
- Keep content file-based and easy to publish.
- Markdown is the default content format. Use MDX only when a specific entry needs embedded components.
- Currently values come from a local config file. `Currently → Writing` is in progress; Recent Writing is published.
- A minimal content-collection setup must exist before homepage Projects/Writing sections are wired to content.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies and browser JavaScript.
- V1 is dark-only. Do not implement a theme switcher.
- Navbar is initially non-sticky.
- MVP footer is copyright, GitHub, LinkedIn, X, and Email only.
- Canonical closing philosophy: “Build. Learn. Document. Improve.”
- GitHub notes, if linked, are a subtle text link, not a homepage card.
- Do not implement decorative vertical slogans or other mockup artifacts literally.

## Visual rules

Follow the approved dark editorial direction:

- spacious
- calm
- technical
- atmospheric
- minimal
- thin borders/dividers
- restrained surfaces/cards
- serif display headings
- clean sans body
- subtle monospace metadata
- muted blue/green/purple/orange accents

Avoid generic flashy developer-portfolio patterns.

## Working style

Make small reviewable changes and implement one section/phase at a time.

Write git commit messages as a single line using conventional commits. Do not add a body.

Before a large departure from the mockup or docs, follow the docs and decision log rather than silently redesigning the site.
